.Language=English,English
.PluginContents=C source browser plugin for FAR

@Contents


^#C Source Browser for FAR (FCSB) v2.1#

   FCSB plugin scans a C programming project or a source file for all
functions and makes a list of these functions with a possibility to move
directly to chosen function in corresponding source file. This list can be
quickly filtered by entering first letters of function's name.
There is a possibility to scan all project "on the wing" or to make
a special project file (fcsbprj$.Far) with a list of all functions.
This project file can be very useful while working with large amount of 
code (some megabytes or dozens of megabytes), but it needs to be 
rebuild from time to time..



^#Menu commands#


#[C functions list]#

   When this menu item is selected from file panel, FCSB searches for
file fcsbprj$.Far in current directory. If this file exists, all function
names are taken from it; otherwise FCSB scans all source files
from the current directory and builds a list of functions in memory.
File mask and subdirectories processing can be changed in plugin settings.
Then You can select any function You want from the list and enter
FAR internal editor. To quit FCSB, simply press ESC. Function list
can be reduced in size by entering first letters of function's name
directly from keyboard. You can enter letters A-Z, figures 0-9, space,
backspace and symbols ':', '_', '~~', '<', '>'. You don't need to press Shift.

   When this menu item is selected from FAR internal editor, FCSB scans
all functions in current file and shows a list of found functions. Then You
can move directly to chosen function by pressing Enter.


#[(Re)scan project]#

   In this case FCSB (re)creates project file fcsbprj$.Far in current
directory. Existing file will be overwritten. This option works only
from file panel. If called from FAR internal editor, it does nothing.



^#Notes#

   Function list by default doesn't include static functions. You can select
what kind of functions (static, inline, class members) You want to include or
exclude from counting.

   While working with a large project, scanning and sorting may last
for some minutes (this plugin was tested with ~~45Mb of source code,
8000 functions, P166, approximate scanning/sorting time - 4 minutes), so it's
a good idea to create a project file with function list. For little
projects (up to 1Mb) this time is approx. 1 second.

   After moving into internal editor from function list it's 
impossible to switch between panels with Ctrl-TAB, because FCSB is
still active :(



